        "main_text_has_explicit_synthesis": true,
        "si_used": false,
        "procedure": "Co2 (50 mg, 0.05 mmol) was dissolved in CH3CN (8 mL), and deaH2 (11 mg, 0.1 mmol) was added while stirring, followed by tBuPO3H2 (14 mg, 0.1 mmol) and NEt3 (40 mg, 0.4 mmol). Gd(NO3)3·6H2O (45 mg, 0.1 mmol) was then added and the mixture was stirred overnight at room temperature. The solution was filtered and the filtrate was kept at room temperature for slow evaporation. Purple block-shaped crystals formed within 3–4 days, were collected by filtration, washed with cold CH3CN, and dried in air.",
